# ============================================================
# Upbit Surge Monitor
# validate_256.py
# Clean V001
# ============================================================
#
# PURPOSE
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Validate outputs generated by:
#
#   detect_256.py - 256 Detector Clean V001
#
# This validator is READ ONLY.
#
# It must NOT:
#
#   - modify OHLCV files
#   - modify Feature files
#   - modify Signal files
#   - create labels
#   - use future price data for signal generation
#   - perform prediction
#   - perform trading
#
#
# CURRENT VALIDATION TARGET
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Market:
#   KRW-BTC
#
# Timeframes:
#   h1
#   h4
#   d1
#
#
# EXPECTED PROJECT STRUCTURE
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# upbit-surge-monitor/
#
#   validate_256.py
#
#   data/
#     ohlcv/
#       h1/KRW-BTC.csv
#       h4/KRW-BTC.csv
#       d1/KRW-BTC.csv
#
#     features/
#       h1/KRW-BTC.csv
#       h4/KRW-BTC.csv
#       d1/KRW-BTC.csv
#
#     signals/
#       256/
#         h1/KRW-BTC.csv
#         h4/KRW-BTC.csv
#         d1/KRW-BTC.csv
#
#
# VALIDATION PRINCIPLES
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# 1. Source files are READ ONLY.
# 2. Signal row count must match Feature row count.
# 3. Signal timestamps must match Feature timestamps.
# 4. Duplicate timestamps are not allowed.
# 5. Timestamp ordering must be chronological.
# 6. OHLCV / Feature / Signal price values are sanity checked.
# 7. SETUP / READY / TRIGGER states are inspected.
# 8. Score columns are inspected when present.
# 9. MA columns are inspected when present.
# 10. Boolean research-condition columns are inspected.
# 11. Suspicious future-information columns are rejected.
# 12. No future-result label is generated here.
#
#
# IMPORTANT
# ------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Clean V001 intentionally discovers optional detector columns
# from the actual Signal CSV instead of inventing column names.
#
# Required structural validation is strict.
#
# Research-column validation is adaptive:
#
#   - if a known MA exists -> validate it
#   - if a score exists -> validate it
#   - if condition/state columns exist -> inspect them
#
# This avoids changing the detector merely to satisfy a validator.
#
# ============================================================


